{"kind":"assert","text":"For the review of authority revision 25 at a1d18e51: the planner has answered its four questions (5a036318). Three confirm the note. One reverses it: the single-controller exception does take effect when the sole controller controls an agent among the authors. Revision 24's condition 3 stands as written (among the authors, or the controller of an agent among them); revision 25 withdrew that clause on a reading of the planner's shorthand, and that withdrawal is wrong. I will restore the clause in the next head of this note, with the planner's act, whatever the verdict on the rest. I leave a1d18e51 as filed so that the review in progress keeps its exact head; please judge the rest and record this as a known correction."}